               <msContents>
                  <summary>Hebrew Bible</summary>
                  <msItem n="1">
                     <title type="desc" key="work_128">Hebrew Bible</title>
                     <title xml:lang="he" key="work_128">תנ"ך</title>
                     <note>Contains the Pentateuch, Joshua, Judges, 1 and 2 Samuel, and Jeremiah.
                        The beginning is defective (the text begins halfway through Genesis 33:7).
                        One excised folio between <locus>ff. 160 and 161</locus> which would have
                        contained Judges 20:47—1 Samuel 3:17; several missing folios between
                           <locus>ff. 200 and 201</locus> which would have contained 2 Samuel
                        24:15—Jeremiah 11:10.</note>
                     <note>With <hi rend="italic">masorah parva</hi> and <hi rend="italic"
                           >magna</hi> throughout.</note>
                     <note>In the prophetic books, the <hi rend="italic">haftarot</hi> corresponding
                        to each of the <hi rend="italic">parashiyot</hi> have been labelled as such
                        by the masorete.</note>
                     <textLang mainLang="he">Hebrew</textLang>
                  </msItem>
               </msContents>
               <physDesc>
                  <objectDesc form="codex">
                     <supportDesc material="perg">
                        <extent>ff. 232 <dimensions type="leaf" unit="mm">
                              <height>450</height>
                              <width>340</width>
                           </dimensions>
                        </extent>
                        <condition>The margins of <locus>f. 1</locus> have been injured, which has
                           resulted in some loss of text in the <hi rend="italic">masorah magna</hi>
                           apparatus along the upper margin.</condition>
                     </supportDesc>
                     <layoutDesc>
                        <layout columns="3">
                           <p>In three columns.</p>
                        </layout>
                     </layoutDesc>
                  </objectDesc>
                  <handDesc>
                     <summary>Ashkenazi square script</summary>
                     <handNote> On <locus>f. 179r</locus>, the name <persName>Shlomoh <foreign
                              xml:lang="he">שלמה</foreign> has been picked out by means of leaves
                           drawn with dotted lines; this was most likely the name of the
                           scribe.</persName>
                     </handNote>
                  </handDesc>
                  <decoDesc>
                     <p>On <locus>ff. 15r, 45r, 67r, 125r, 143v</locus>, the enlarged initial words
                        of the biblical books are decorated with simple scalloped borders and
                        foliate finials. The penwoprk-decorated initial word for Deuteronomy at
                           <locus>f. 97v</locus> was most likely a later addition.</p>
                     <p>Simple, geometric drawings next to the catchwords.</p>
                     <p>Some of the <hi rend="italic">masorah magna</hi> have been written in
                        micrography, forming simple geometric shapes.</p>
                  </decoDesc>
                  <bindingDesc>
                     <p>Brown leather with an embossed grain and blind-tooled decorations (including
                        elaborate central medallions, featuring interlaced strapwork typical of
                        sixteenth-century bindings, on both upper and lower boards), over thick
                        wooden bevelled boards. A diamond-shaped paper slip is glued to the top of
                        the spine, where the former shelfmark (84) has been written by hand.</p>
                     <condition>Two clasps now missing.</condition>
                  </bindingDesc>
               </physDesc>
